>$20$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$60$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Let $B$ be the event that a randomly selected student is a <strong>&quot;Boy&quot;</strong>, and $C$ be the event that a randomly selected student has <strong>&quot;Brown&quot;</strong> eyes. Estimate $P(B\\cap C).$</p>\n","choice1":"$ \\dfrac{3}{20}$","choice2":"$ \\dfrac{2}{15}$","choice3":"$ \\dfrac{11}{100}$","choice4":"$ \\dfrac{13}{100}$","choice5":"$ \\dfrac{1}{50}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, note that $B\\cap C$ is the event that a randomly selected student is a boy and has brown eyes. </p>\n<p>To estimate the probability of $B \\cap C,$ we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>find the number at the intersection of the row <strong>&quot;Boys&quot;</strong> and the column <strong>&quot;Brown&quot;</strong>, and then</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The number at the intersection of the row <strong>&quot;Boys&quot;</strong> and the column <strong>&quot;Brown&quot;</strong> is highlighted in the table below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Green</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Blue</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Brown</td>\n<td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Black</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Girls</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$40$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Boys</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}15$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$60$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(100),$ we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n    P(B\\cap C) = \\dfrac{15}{100} =  \\dfrac{3}{20}.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data"},"example":{"id":5105,"title":"Estimating the Probability of the Intersection of Events"},"group":{"id":79397,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241642,"answer":{"id":62263991,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:54:04.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12861},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264023,"created":"2026-10-15T12:54:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12116,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:54 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":74424,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":5105,"text":"<p>Dana surveys $72$ randomly chosen students at her school, asking them if they have gerbils or rabbits at home. Her findings are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Has a rabbit</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t have a rabbit</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Has a gerbil</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t have a gerbil</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$36$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$42$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$48$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$72$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Estimate the probability that a randomly chosen student at the school has a gerbil and also has a rabbit.</p>\n","choice1":"$0.25$","choice2":"$0.17$","choice3":"$0.08$","choice4":"$0.50$","choice5":"$0.42$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To estimate the probability that a randomly chosen student at the school has a gerbil and also has a rabbit, we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>find the number at the intersection of the row <strong>&quot;Has a gerbil&quot;</strong> and the column <strong>&quot;Has a rabbit&quot;</strong>, and then</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The number at the intersection of the row <strong>&quot;Has a gerbil&quot;</strong> and the column <strong>&quot;Has a rabbit&quot;</strong> is highlighted in the table below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Has a rabbit</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t have a rabbit</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Has a gerbil</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}18$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t have a gerbil</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$36$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$42$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$48$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$72$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(72),$ we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n    p = \\dfrac{18}{72} = 0.25.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data"},"example":{"id":5105,"title":"Estimating the Probability of the Intersection of Events"},"group":{"id":79395,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241642,"answer":{"id":62264023,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:54:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12116},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":5104,"number":2,"title":"Estimating the Probability of the Union of Events","answers":[{"id":62264061,"created":"2026-10-15T12:54:45.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13108,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:54 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":46814,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":5104,"text":"<p>Martin surveyed some students in a school, asking them if they have cats or dogs at home. His findings are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Has a dog</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t have a dog</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\"> Has a cat </td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t have a cat</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$ 10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$17$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$ 32$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n\n<p>Estimate the probability that a randomly chosen student in the school has either a cat or a dog but not both.</p>\n","choice1":"$\\dfrac{19}{32}$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{1}{32}$","choice3":"$\\dfrac{1}{19}$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{5}{19}$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{29}{32}$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>To estimate the probability that a randomly chosen student in the school has either a cat or a dog but not both, we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>add up the numbers in the row <strong>&quot; Has a cat&quot;</strong> or the column <strong>&quot;Has a dog&quot;</strong> but not in their intersection, and</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The numbers in the row <strong>&quot;Has a cat&quot;</strong> or the column <strong>&quot;Has a dog&quot;</strong> but not in their intersection are highlighted below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Has a dog</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t have a dog</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\"> Has a cat </td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}9$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t have a cat</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$ \\color{blue}10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$17$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$ 32$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Adding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(32),$ we get</p>\n<p>\\[\np = \\dfrac{9+10}{32} = \\dfrac{19}{32}.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data"},"example":{"id":5104,"title":"Estimating the Probability of the Union of Events"},"group":{"id":79393,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241642,"answer":{"id":62264061,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:54:45.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13108},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264109,"created":"2026-10-15T12:55:01.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12356,"number":4,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:55 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":47137,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":5104,"text":"<p>A randomly selected group of students from a high school were asked about their favorite sport between baseball, football, basketball, or soccer. The results of the survey are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Baseball</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Football</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Basketball</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Soccer</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Girls</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$19$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$51$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Boys</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$49$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$32$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Let $F$ be the event that a randomly selected student in the high school is a <strong>&quot;Girl&quot;</strong> whose favorite sport is <strong>&quot;Football&quot;</strong>, and $S$ be the event that a randomly selected student in the high school is a <strong>&quot;Girl&quot;</strong> whose favorite sport is <strong>&quot;Soccer&quot;</strong>. Estimate $P(F\\cup S).$</p>\n","choice1":"$0.31$","choice2":"$0.41$","choice3":"$0.79$","choice4":"$0.59$","choice5":"$0.51$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, note that $F \\cup S$ is the event that a randomly selected student in the high school is a girl whose favorite sport is football or a girl whose favorite sport is soccer. </p>\n<p>To estimate the probability of $F \\cup S,$ we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>add up the numbers in the columns <strong>&quot;Football&quot;</strong> or <strong>&quot;Soccer&quot;</strong> and the row <strong>&quot;Girls&quot;</strong>, and</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The numbers in the columns <strong>&quot;Football&quot;</strong> or <strong>&quot;Soccer&quot;</strong> and the row <strong>&quot;Girls&quot;</strong> are highlighted below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Baseball</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Football</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Basketball</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Soccer</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Girls</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}19$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}12$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$51$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Boys</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$49$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$32$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Adding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(100),$ we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n   P(F \\cup S) =\\dfrac{19+12}{100} = \\dfrac{31}{100} = 0.31.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data"},"example":{"id":5104,"title":"Estimating the Probability of the Union of Events"},"group":{"id":79394,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241642,"answer":{"id":62264109,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:55:01.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12356},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264128,"created":"2026-10-15T12:55:17.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12839,"number":5,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:55 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":47141,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":5104,"text":"<p>In a high school, a group of students was asked about whether they prefer apples, oranges, or bananas. The results are given in the two-way frequency table below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Apple</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Orange</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Banana</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Girls</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$26$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Boys</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$50$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Estimate the probability that a randomly chosen student in the group preferred apples or bananas or is a girl.  </p>\n","choice1":" $0.88$","choice2":" $0.12$","choice3":" $0.52$","choice4":" $0.46$","choice5":" $0.26$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To estimate the probability that a randomly chosen student preferred apples or bananas or is a girl, we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>add up the numbers in the columns <strong>&quot;Apple&quot;</strong> or <strong>&quot;Banana&quot;</strong> or the row <strong>&quot;Girls&quot;</strong>, and</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The numbers in the columns <strong>&quot;Apple&quot;</strong> or <strong>&quot;Banana&quot;</strong> or the row <strong>&quot;Girls&quot;</strong> are highlighted below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Apple</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Orange</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Banana</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Girls</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#FFF8E5\" align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}11$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#FFF8E5\" align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}8$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#FFF8E5\" align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}7$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$26$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Boys</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#FFF8E5\" align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}12$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td bgcolor=\"#FFF8E5\" align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}6$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$50$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Adding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(50),$ we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n   p=\\dfrac{11+12+8+7+6}{50} = \\dfrac{44}{50} = 0.88.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data"},"example":{"id":5104,"title":"Estimating the Probability of the Union of Events"},"group":{"id":79393,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241642,"answer":{"id":62264128,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:55:17.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12839},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264185,"created":"2026-10-15T12:55:35.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12344,"number":6,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:55 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":120355,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":5104,"text":"<p>Some customers in a pizzeria were asked about the type of pizza they prefer between spicy pizza and vegetarian pizza. The results of the survey are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.</p>\n<p><table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black\" rules=all cellpadding=5></p>\n<p><tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Prefers Spicy</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Prefers  Vegetarian</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\"> Children </td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$22$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$32$</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Adults</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$41$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$27$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$68$</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$51$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$49$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n<br></p>\n<p>Estimate the probability that a randomly chosen person is an adult or prefers spicy pizza (or both).</p>\n","choice1":"$0.78$","choice2":"$0.68$","choice3":"$0.37$","choice4":"$0.51$","choice5":"$0.28$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To estimate the probability that a randomly chosen person is an adult or prefers spicy pizza, we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>add up the numbers in the row <strong>&quot;Adults&quot;</strong> or the column <strong>&quot;Prefers Spicy&quot;</strong>, and</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The numbers in the row <strong>&quot;Adults&quot;</strong> or the column <strong>&quot;Prefers Spicy&quot;</strong> are highlighted below.</p>\n<p><table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black\" rules=all cellpadding=5></p>\n<p><tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Prefers Spicy</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Prefers Vegetarian</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\"> Children </td>\n <td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}10$</td> \n  <td align=\"center\">$22$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$32$</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Adults</td></p>\n<p><td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}41$</td> </p>\n<p><td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}27$</td> \n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$68$</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$51$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$49$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n<br></p>\n<p>Adding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(100),$ we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n   p=\\dfrac{10+41+27}{100} = \\dfrac{78}{100} = 0.78.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data"},"example":{"id":5104,"title":"Estimating the Probability of the Union of Events"},"group":{"id":79393,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241642,"answer":{"id":62264185,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:55:35.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12344},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":5106,"number":3,"title":"Estimating Using Probabilities","answers":[{"id":62264221,"created":"2026-10-15T12:55:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13472,"number":7,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:55 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":47294,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":5106,"text":"<p>Roger surveyed $62$ Jefferson High School students. He asked them if they like biology and chemistry. His findings are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.</p>\n<p><table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black\" rules=all cellpadding=5></p>\n<p><tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Like biology</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t like biology</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\"> Like chemistry </td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$19$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$44$</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t like chemistry</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$33$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$29$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$62$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n<br></p>\n<p>Edison High School has $500$ students. Assuming that the distribution of the results is the same in both high schools, determine the number of Edison High School students who like biology or chemistry but not both. Round your answer to the nearest integer.</p>\n","choice1":"$218$","choice2":"$230$","choice3":"$250$","choice4":"$240$","choice5":"$205$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To estimate the number of students who like biology or chemistry but not both, we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>add up the numbers in the row <strong>&quot;Like chemistry&quot;</strong> or the column <strong>&quot; Like biology&quot;</strong>, but not in both, and then</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black\" rules=all cellpadding=5></p>\n<p><tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Like biology</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t like biology</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\"> Like chemistry </td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}19$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$44$</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Doesn&#39;t like chemistry</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}8$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n</tr></p>\n<p><tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$33$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$29$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$62$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n<br></p>\n<p>Adding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(62),$ we get</p>\n<p>\\[\np = \\dfrac{8+19}{62} = \\dfrac{27}{62} = 0.435.\n\\]</p>\n<p>This represents the estimated probability that a randomly selected student likes biology or chemistry but not both.</p>\n<p>Finally, to find the estimated number of students of Edison High School who like biology or chemistry but not both, we multiply the total number of students in the Edison High School $(500)$ by the probability above:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nn &=500 \\cdot p \\\\[3pt]\n&= 500 \\cdot 0.435 \\\\[3pt]\n&= 217.5 \\\\[3pt]\n& = 218,\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nrounded to the nearest integer.</p>\n","topic":{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data"},"example":{"id":5106,"title":"Estimating Using Probabilities"},"group":{"id":79399,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241642,"answer":{"id":62264221,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:55:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13472},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264261,"created":"2026-10-15T12:56:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13870,"number":8,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:56 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":47138,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":5106,"text":"<p>A group of randomly selected students from School A was asked about whether or not they use TV or the internet to access the local news. The results of the survey are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">TV</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">No TV</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Internet</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$90$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$105$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">No internet</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$45$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$120$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$150$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>There are $100$ students in School B. Assuming that the distribution of the results is the same for both schools, \nestimate the number of School B students that access the local news either from TV or the internet, but not both.</p>\n","choice1":" $30$","choice2":" $20$","choice3":" $70$","choice4":" $80$","choice5":" $40$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To estimate the probability that a randomly selected student gets the local news either from TV or the internet but not both, we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>add up the numbers in the row <strong>&quot;No internet&quot;</strong> or the column <strong>&quot;TV&quot;</strong>, but not in both, and then</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">TV</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">No TV</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Internet</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$90$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#FFF8E5\" align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}15$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$105$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">No internet</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#FFF8E5\" align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}30$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$45$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$120$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$150$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Adding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(150),$ we get</p>\n<p>\\[\np = \\dfrac{30+15}{150} = \\dfrac{45}{150} = 0.3.\n\\]</p>\n<p>This represents the estimated probability that a randomly selected student gets the local news from TV or the internet but not both.</p>\n<p>Finally, to find the estimated number of students of School B that get their local news either from TV or the internet but not both, we multiply the total number of students in the school $(100)$ by the probability above:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nn &=100 \\cdot p \\\\[3pt]\n&= 100 \\cdot 0.3 \\\\[3pt]\n&= 30\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data"},"example":{"id":5106,"title":"Estimating Using Probabilities"},"group":{"id":79398,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241642,"answer":{"id":62264261,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:56:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13870},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264281,"created":"2026-10-15T12:56:33.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12168,"number":9,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:56 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":120744,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":5106,"text":"<p>A group of randomly selected customers from a certain insurance company was asked about the type of vehicle driven and whether they received a speeding ticket in the last year. The results of the survey are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">SUV</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Sport car</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Speeding ticket</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$80$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$85$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">No speeding ticket</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$110$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>There are $220$ drivers in another insurance company. Assuming that the distribution of the results is the same for both companies, estimate the number of drivers in the second insurance company that drive SUV or received a speeding ticket, but not both.</p>\n","choice1":"$50$","choice2":"$40$","choice3":"$45$","choice4":"$55$","choice5":"$60$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To estimate the probability that a randomly selected driver drives the SUV or received a speeding ticket but not both, we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>add up the numbers in the row <strong>&quot;Speeding ticket&quot;</strong> or the column <strong>&quot;SUV&quot;</strong>, but not in both, and then</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=all cellpadding=5>\n<tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">SUV</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Sport car</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Speeding ticket</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#FFF8E5\" align=\"center\">$80$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}5$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$85$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">No speeding ticket</td>\n  <td align=\"center\">$\\color{blue}20$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#FFF8E5\" align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$110$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n\n\n<p>Adding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(110),$ we get</p>\n<p>\\[\np = \\dfrac{20+5}{110} = \\dfrac{5}{22}.\n\\]</p>\n<p>This represents the estimated probability that a randomly selected driver drives an SUV or received a speeding ticket but not both.</p>\n<p>Finally, to find the estimated number of drivers in the second company that drive SUVs or received a speeding ticket, but not both, we multiply the total number of drivers in the company $(220)$ by the probability above:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nn &=220 \\cdot p \\\\[3pt]\n&= 220 \\cdot  \\dfrac{5}{22} \\\\[3pt]\n&= 50\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data"},"example":{"id":5106,"title":"Estimating Using Probabilities"},"group":{"id":79399,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241642,"answer":{"id":62264281,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:56:33.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12168},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]}],"localGraph":{"topicId":131,"topics":[{"id":131,"name":"Compound Events in Probability From Experimental Data","prerequisites":[2826,2827,7220],"frontier":0,"halfLife":11.16122891807224,"repetition":3,"stability":0.4001280213415675},{"id":794,"name":"Computing Probabilities for Compound Events Using Venn Diagrams","prerequisites":[131],"frontier":1,"halfLife":0.1,"repetition":0,"stability":0},{"id":1133,"name":"Conditional Probabilities From Two-Way Frequency Tables","prerequisites":[131]},{"id":2826,"name":"The Union of Sets","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":7.218278305214673,"repetition":3,"stability":0.3407568568100121},{"id":2827,"name":"The Intersection of Sets","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":4.866430527051557,"repetition":2,"stability":0.29442504606391634},{"id":7220,"name":"Using Experimental Probability to Make Predictions","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":2.8953142308965467,"repetition":2,"stability":0.24239466346030866}]}}}